# broiler-shared-package pin 1
#
# One package of the committed, hash-pinned feed (decision SJL-D-4 (c); milestone SJL-2.7): a shared
# JavaScript library package whose home is the Broiler.JS repository, retained here byte for byte so
# that a restore needs no other repository's folder and no network for it. NuGet.config's package
# source mapping sends the Broiler.ECMAScript prefix to this directory and to nuget.org; the lock
# file of a project that references it records `content-hash`, and rule I1 holds that hash to this
# pin and to the allow-list.
#
# HOW IT WAS TAKEN. The package exactly as the Broiler.JS repository's publish-shared workflow pushed
# it to nuget.org on 2026-10-17 (run 39064131506, its artifact shared-packages), packed from
# `upstream-commit`; the nuspec's repository element records the same commit, which rule I7 reads.
# nuget.org serves the same package with its repository signature (.signature.p7s) added, and NuGet's
# content hash of a signed package leaves the signature out, so a restore from either source records
# `content-hash`, the base64 SHA-512 of this file's bytes. `sha256` is over the same bytes.
#
# (Revised 2026-10-17, when the package was published. Until then this feed held a copy packed locally
# from Broiler.JS 2d37a38. Between 2d37a38 and the published commit nothing under Broiler.ECMAScript/
# changes but the changelog and the source's version suffix, which the workflow's version overrides, so
# the library code is the same; the package differs in the commit its nuspec and assembly record, the
# identifiers derived from them, the case of the repository URL, and the branch the nuspec names. The
# paragraph read: "Packed on 2026-10-17 in the Broiler.JS repository, from `upstream-commit`, in a clean
# checkout of it, with `dotnet pack Broiler.ECMAScript/Broiler.ECMAScript.Algorithms -c Release
# -p:ContinuousIntegrationBuild=true`; Broiler.ECMAScript/Directory.Build.props sets the version,
# 0.1.0-preview.5, at that commit. The nuspec's repository element records the same commit, which rule I7
# reads. `content-hash` is NuGet's: the base64 SHA-512 of the .nupkg's bytes, which is what a lock file
# records. `sha256` is over the same bytes. It is not on nuget.org: a Broiler.VM package release that
# depends on it waits for its publication (eng/verify-feed.ps1), and the pin is then taken again from the
# published package, as 0.1.0-preview.4's was." The identity lines read:
#   content-hash 36JEduY8/4RoKije2K2laopa7bwb6ULQLKyXDUkm1795zXv995v+ez63UhO5p0Xe08fadyVMVn822lK8vGYqfQ==
#   sha256 f5896e57b9db11a400bf03edd084af5783e21d7df549370b84c00cb292cf86be
#   upstream-commit 2d37a38a2560b076ebf2ca29989bfe20db64ed64)
#
# WHAT IT IS. The time-zone and calendar area of the shared algorithms library (milestone SJL-8.3;
# Broiler.VM's JSD-0076), namespace Broiler.ECMAScript.Time - the decoder of the time-zone and
# calendar tables an engine hands in, identifier lookup and primary identifiers, offsets and
# transitions, possible instants, disambiguation, the start of a day, the offset time zones and the
# Chinese, Korean, Umm al-Qura and Persian years - beside the number-conversion, numerics, text and
# Date areas of 0.1.0-preview.4, unchanged: admitted for PRODUCT use by Broiler.VM.Profile.JavaScript
# and Broiler.VM.Profile.JavaScript.Compiler at SJL-8.5, and restored by the admission probe. Beside
# 0.1.0-preview.4's components it carries one more, a C# port of ICU4X's lunisolar approximation
# (icu_calendar 2.3.0's src/cal/east_asian_traditional/simple.rs, Unicode-3.0), which its
# THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md names with the licence text; the port is the one Broiler.VM's JsCalendars
# carried until this family's cut-over. It carries no table: the time-zone and calendar tables are
# data each engine embeds (decision SJL-D-6 (c)). It is on nuget.org since 2026-10-17, as a Broiler.VM
# package release that depends on it requires (eng/verify-feed.ps1).

id Broiler.ECMAScript.Algorithms
version 0.1.0-preview.5
file Broiler.ECMAScript.Algorithms.0.1.0-preview.5.nupkg
content-hash fi/eRdQ5I2CUFg/HTWX0Js03+rgPwDK4+0q5x4AvM3Aqi57mkxz9Z0ykwuXNYe6Cd/h67+6pZcBwcVokD0FLmA==
sha256 b6764147bd0a8edb17369f3b419c1d6664b82b091ba9312e45fa331082bdf69e
upstream Broiler-Platform/broiler.js
upstream-commit a04cd447af3424951eb767524812b5b310d71da3
